# m.below reads the pixels already drawn under a node, 256x128 on paper, two rows of three cells.
# The brush smudge, declared in this file, mixes the paint halfway toward what is under it,
# weighted by that backdrop's alpha, so over paper or gold the color is the mean of the two and
# over nothing (inside a fresh layer) the paint stays as it is. Every brushed square is blue
# p.blue.2 and every backdrop square is gold p.gold.2.
# Row 1 (y 32). Cell 1 (x 16..88): a gold square at x 16..64 and a smudged blue square at
# x 40..88 over its right half. The blue square's left half, over gold, is an even olive green
# (half blue, half gold); its right half, over paper, is an even pale blue; the gold square's
# left part stays gold. Cell 2 (x 101..173): the same two squares, but the blue one is inside a
# layer and the gold one is not. The blue square is plain blue over both halves: the layer
# starts from nothing, so the brush sees no gold and no paper. Cell 3 (x 189..245): a gold
# square at x 193..241 with a smudged blue stroke 8 wide on its edge. The inner half of the
# stroke, over the fill, is olive green; the outer half, over paper, is pale blue; the gold
# inside stays gold.
# Row 2 (y 96). Cell 4 (x 16..88): the squares of cell 1 with an ink band 12 tall across the
# middle of the blue square as its child. The band is solid ink over both halves and stops at
# the blue square's edges; the blue square around it reads as in cell 1. Cell 5 (x 101..173):
# the squares of cell 1 with the blue square at a:.5. The blue square is half as strong: its
# left half is gold tinted a little toward blue, its right half paper tinted a little toward
# blue. Cell 6 (x 181..253): the squares of cell 1 with brush:[smudge dim], where dim, also
# declared here, keeps 60% of the color it is handed. The whole stack runs over the backdrop
# once smudge reads it, so the left half is cell 1's olive darkened to 60% and the right half
# is cell 1's pale blue darkened to 60%; dim darkens the mix, not the blue alone.
# Every edge is antialiased; nothing is drawn outside its squares.
@artboard 256x128
@target brush/below.png

brush smudge k:.5
  sksl """
  float4 shade(Mark m) {
    return float4(mix(m.paint.rgb, m.below.rgb, m.below.a * k), cover(m.edge, m));
  }
  """

brush dim
  sksl """
  float4 shade(Mark m) {
    return float4(m.paint.rgb * .6, cover(m.edge, m));
  }
  """

rect 48 at:40,32 fill:p.gold.2
rect 48 at:64,32 fill:p.blue.2 brush:smudge name:over_gold

rect 48 at:125,32 fill:p.gold.2
layer fresh
  rect 48 at:149,32 fill:p.blue.2 brush:smudge name:in_layer

rect 48 at:217,32 fill:p.gold.2 stroke:p.blue.2,8 brush:smudge(on:stroke) name:edge

rect 48 at:40,96 fill:p.gold.2
rect 48 at:64,96 fill:p.blue.2 brush:smudge name:with_child
  rect 72,12 fill:p.ink

rect 48 at:125,96 fill:p.gold.2
rect 48 at:149,96 fill:p.blue.2 brush:smudge a:.5 name:faint

rect 48 at:205,96 fill:p.gold.2
rect 48 at:229,96 fill:p.blue.2 brush:[smudge dim] name:stacked
